.Dd April 25, 2026
.Dt CSTOW 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cstow
.Nd manage software packages using symlinks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm cstow
.Op Fl cDhnRSov
.Op Fl d Ar directory
.Op Fl t Ar directory
.Ar package
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs a package by creating symbolic links.
Only files are symlinked; directories are created as needed.
.Pp
A
.Em package
is a directory containing a standard file hierarchy as described in
.Xr hier 7 .
A
.Em package depot
is a directory containing multiple packages as subdirectories.
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
looks for
.Ar package
in the current directory and symlinks its contents into its parent
directory.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Report all conflicts instead of stopping at the first one.
Implies
.Fl n .
.It Fl D
Uninstall
.Ar package .
Removes all symbolic links that point into the package and any directories that
become empty.
.It Fl d Ar directory
Use
.Ar directory
as the depot.
By default, the current directory is used.
If specified more than once, the last value is used.
.It Fl h
Display a usage message and exit.
.It Fl n
Dry run. 
Check for conflicts without modifying the file system.
.It Fl o
Enable dotfile translation.
When a file or directory name starts with
.Dq dot. ,
replace that prefix with a literal dot in the target link name.
The same
.Fl o
flag must be used when uninstalling the package.
.It Fl R
Reinstall
.Ar package .
Equivalent to
.Nm Fl D
followed by an install.
.It Fl S
Install
.Ar package .
Implied if neither
.Fl D
nor
.Fl R
are used.
.It Fl t Ar directory
Use
.Ar directory
as the target.
If not specified, the parent of the depot is used.
If multiple
.Fl t
flags are given, the last value is used.
.It Fl v
Be verbose.
Print each operation to standard output.
.El
.Pp
Trailing slashes in
.Ar package
are ignored.
.Pp
A conflict occurs when a symlink already exists in the target directory.
.Nm
will exit with an error unless
.Fl n
or
.Fl c
are given.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Assume the current directory is a package depot.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Install a package:
.Dl $ Nm cstow Ar pkg
.It Uninstall a package:
.Dl $ Nm cstow Fl D Ar pkg
.It Reinstall a package after its contents have changed:
.Dl $ Nm cstow Fl R Ar pkg
.It Use an explicit depot and target:
.Dl $ Nm cstow Fl d Ar /var/cstow Fl t Ar /opt Ar pkg
.It Check for conflicts without modifying anything:
.Dl $ Nm cstow Fl n Ar pkg
.It Install with dotfile translation:
.Dl $ Nm cstow Fl o Ar pkg
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hier 7 ,
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Adolfo Perez Alvarez Aq Mt adolfopa@sdf.org
.Sh BUGS
Uninstalling a package that contains symbolic links may fail.
During uninstall,
.Nm
follows the full symbolic link chain when verifying ownership.
If a file is a symbolic link whose final target points outside the depot,
.Nm
will refuse to remove the corresponding installed link,
reporting it as foreign to the package.
